1	SOP: Bug Triage and Technical Issue Handling	# SOP: Bug Triage and Technical Issue Handling\n\n## Overview\nThis document defines how support agents triage, document, and escalate bug reports and technical issues.\n\n## Severity Classification\n\n### P0 — Critical (respond in 15 minutes)\n- Platform completely down for one or more customers\n- Data loss or data corruption confirmed\n- Security vulnerability actively exploited\n- Payment processing failure\n\n### P1 — High (respond in 1 hour)\n- Core feature broken for a customer segment\n- Integration failure affecting active workflows\n- Performance degradation > 50% vs baseline\n- Bug introduced by a recent deployment\n\n### P2 — Medium (respond in 4 hours)\n- Non-core feature broken with workaround available\n- Browser-specific rendering issue\n- API returning unexpected response for edge case\n\n### P3 — Low (respond in 1 business day)\n- Cosmetic UI issue\n- Minor copy or formatting error\n- Feature behaving unexpectedly but not blocking workflow\n\n## Triage Process\n\n### Step 1 — Reproduce the issue\n1. Confirm browser, OS, and app version\n2. Ask for console logs if browser-based issue\n3. Ask for API request/response payload if API issue\n4. Confirm if issue is consistent or intermittent\n5. Check if issue started after a specific date (correlate with deployments)\n\n### Step 2 — Check for existing reports\n1. Search internal bug tracker for duplicate reports\n2. Check status page for ongoing incidents\n3. If known issue: inform customer with ETA and workaround\n\n### Step 3 — Escalate to Engineering\nRequired information for Engineering ticket:\n- Steps to reproduce (numbered, precise)\n- Expected vs actual behavior\n- Browser/OS/version details\n- Console logs or error messages\n- Customer tier and MRR (prioritization signal)\n- Deployment date correlation if identified\n\n## Workarounds by Issue Type\n\n### Safari rendering issues\n- Ask customer to disable Safari extensions\n- Try Private Browsing mode\n- Suggest Chrome or Firefox as temporary workaround\n\n### API errors\n- Confirm API key is valid and not expired\n- Check rate limit headers in response\n- Verify request payload matches current API spec (docs.luminnoz.com/api)\n\n## Tone Guidelines\n- Always validate the customer's frustration — bugs are our fault, not theirs\n- Provide a workaround before escalating — never leave customer blocked\n- Set realistic fix ETAs — underpromise, overdeliver\n- Follow up proactively when fix is deployed — do not wait for customer to ask\n	bug_report	[-0.07847901,-0.0052368813,0.03316196,-0.01425415,0.057450544,-0.07549513,-0.05431012,0.015623449,-0.07186288,0.001510592,0.030672722,-0.030746883,-0.056986347,-0.0018487746,0.09569871,0.031607017,0.081021756,-0.078327246,-0.044830542,0.018765878,-0.0067005404,0.008052541,-0.08062864,0.071490675,-0.063147604,0.03980048,-0.039731953,-0.046255276,-0.023545418,-0.07124322,-0.018073363,0.06202283,-0.09918972,-0.001172224,0.08813193,0.045986313,0.027598368,-0.029673314,-0.03052635,-0.019965054,0.0042100637,-0.07637162,-0.08550593,0.0037077272,0.047583673,-0.06402336,-0.018332863,-0.00840603,-0.060293917,0.0016425388,-0.05291332,0.028845333,0.013865189,0.012578057,-0.042918682,0.0054175965,0.04662268,-0.0018848386,0.008479087,0.04478008,0.034776315,-0.06440682,0.01891674,0.041175015,0.02615381,0.078572094,-0.00077833515,-0.088309065,-0.0018863624,-0.01789846,-0.046567958,-0.009403891,-0.10665116,0.003482972,0.011435074,-0.010327748,-0.0059903893,0.01841959,-0.0009404328,-0.093697675,0.011609291,-0.021915602,-0.023193143,0.09534291,0.052751817,0.019292215,-0.015598461,0.06736604,-0.02847438,-0.030548124,0.051320817,0.0035423005,0.09908392,0.03783268,0.06493171,0.029833728,0.034682527,-0.10574207,-0.06549494,0.025941128,-0.01994137,-0.021252505,0.041987404,0.010480147,0.046754573,0.0161093,0.0100618005,0.036777712,0.03756587,0.014427835,-0.027395518,0.0018458964,0.01695478,-0.07868921,0.067588516,0.015778141,0.0010994225,0.0209910