2	SOP: Cancellation and Retention	# SOP: Cancellation and Retention\n\n## Overview\nThis document defines how support agents handle cancellation requests and execute retention strategies.\n\n## Cancellation Request Triage\n\n### Step 1 — Identify the reason\nAlways ask (or infer from ticket) the primary cancellation reason:\n- Price / budget constraints\n- Missing features\n- Switching to a competitor\n- Low usage / not seeing value\n- Dissatisfaction with support\n\n### Step 2 — Qualify retention potential\nHigh retention potential:\n- Customer has been active in the last 30 days\n- Cancellation reason is price or missing features (addressable)\n- Customer has a CSM assigned\n- Account age > 6 months\n\nLow retention potential:\n- Customer has not logged in for 60+ days\n- Competitor already selected and contract signed\n- Multiple unresolved complaints in history\n\n## Retention Playbook\n\n### Price objection\n1. Acknowledge the concern without being defensive\n2. Offer options in this order:\n   - Annual plan discount (up to 20% — no approval needed)\n   - Temporary pause (up to 2 months — Growth and above)\n   - Downgrade to lower tier (retain the customer at lower MRR)\n3. For Enterprise: escalate to CSM before making any offer\n\n### Missing features objection\n1. Confirm exactly which features are missing\n2. Check internal roadmap — if feature is in next 2 quarters, share ETA\n3. Offer workaround if available\n4. If feature is not on roadmap: be honest, do not over-promise\n\n### Competitor objection\n1. Do not disparage the competitor\n2. Highlight Luminnoz differentiators relevant to their use case\n3. Offer a 30-day extension to complete evaluation\n\n## Escalation\n- Enterprise cancellation → always escalate to CSM before responding\n- MRR > $1,000 → loop in Support Lead\n- Customer mentions contract termination → escalate to VP Customer Success\n\n## Tone Guidelines\n- Never make the customer feel guilty for leaving\n- Be genuinely helpful — sometimes the right answer is to let them go\n- Always leave the door open: "We'd love to have you back"\n- Do not use retention scripts verbatim — personalize every response\n	cancellation	[-0.032851424,0.07017826,-0.0019608126,0.033286586,0.008032884,0.07618903,0.02151536,0.011097365,0.013259162,0.0043972144,0.09898421,-0.0022211482,0.010094608,-0.05962866,0.0709936,-0.0022319418,0.0011084448,-0.032497063,-0.03893094,0.0017152652,-0.027738862,-0.040785618,-0.062093113,0.064374626,-0.029593637,-0.023199132,0.06392742,0.047148492,-0.045156036,-0.034889225,0.027619883,0.09174776,0.024056172,-0.03630152,0.037526757,-0.0037063984,-0.09651699,-0.05752574,-0.04737238,-0.024885038,-0.012726268,-0.036867578,-0.11593697,-0.04192974,0.014653399,-0.009784657,-0.08494906,-0.0012859425,-0.024733093,0.06852794,0.05035544,-0.02416192,-0.029353604,0.018862091,-0.076752625,0.04349608,0.01458277,-0.022043232,-0.05148789,-0.03814954,-0.012328187,-0.09836343,-0.023079917,0.024940792,-0.08024771,0.035112925,-0.0006319464,-0.026976092,0.006479418,0.05245715,-0.054102834,-0.074831225,-0.08800469,0.028566312,-0.018694691,0.06820052,0.0965136,0.01632577,0.0959146,-0.06168062,-0.039759815,-0.016831188,-0.062391803,-0.0014989262,-0.05095874,-0.03804455,0.023112891,0.024198828,-0.020628354,-0.012823575,0.15308075,0.029228717,0.0058323657,-0.041774083,-0.046248727,0.02497897,-0.052982513,-0.049400546,-0.03775543,0.021163661,0.03866978,0.02549584,-0.0053793434,-0.015602254,-0.05832959,-0.079090774,-0.006835315,0.034338642,0.0608942,0.029031599,-0.048063394,-0.07455471,0.03267614,0.029157864,0.030979287,0.1303982,-0.0050080996,0.05022552,0.08791232,-0.038116116,0.038929436,0.093171455,-0.00836468,-0.012630708,-0.038313594,0.021562273,-0.010354729,1.0583599e-32,-0.033652414,0.0053543546,-0.07245861,-0.046324685,0.046010632,-0.07306037,0.050882842,0.050900918,-0.07251226,0.04459203,-0.02387174,0.039552066,-0.0030752097,-0.03453398,-0.031512257,-0.10019568,0.018172594,0.10728373,0.057045456,0.02006517,0.0716