3	SOP: Escalation Protocol	# SOP: Escalation Protocol\n\n## Overview\nThis document defines when and how to escalate tickets to senior support, management, or other teams.\n\n## Escalation Tiers\n\n### Tier 1 — Senior Support Agent\nTrigger when:\n- Customer has sent more than 2 follow-up messages without resolution\n- Ticket unresolved after 4 business hours (enterprise) or 8 hours (growth/starter)\n- Customer expresses strong frustration or dissatisfaction\n\n### Tier 2 — Support Lead\nTrigger when:\n- Customer explicitly requests to speak with a manager\n- Customer mentions legal action, chargeback, or contract termination\n- Enterprise account with unresolved billing dispute after 2 hours\n- Ticket involves a potential data breach or security concern\n\n### Tier 3 — VP Customer Success + Legal\nTrigger when:\n- Customer sends formal written notice of legal action\n- Chargeback has been filed with the bank\n- Potential regulatory or compliance violation identified\n- Enterprise contract termination threatened by C-level contact\n\n## Escalation Process\n\n### Step 1 — Document before escalating\n- Summarize the issue in 2–3 sentences\n- List all actions taken so far\n- Note customer tier, MRR, and account age\n- Flag if customer has a CSM assigned\n\n### Step 2 — Notify the customer\n- Inform the customer that their ticket has been escalated\n- Provide a realistic response time commitment\n- Do not promise outcomes you cannot guarantee\n\n### Step 3 — Hand off in the ticketing system\n- Assign ticket to escalation owner\n- Add internal note with full context\n- Set follow-up reminder for 1 hour\n\n## Response Time SLAs by Tier\n| Customer Tier | First Response | Resolution Target |\n|---------------|---------------|-------------------|\n| Enterprise    | 1 hour        | 4 hours           |\n| Growth        | 4 hours       | 8 hours           |\n| Starter       | 8 hours       | 24 hours          |\n\n## Tone Guidelines\n- Never tell a customer their issue is "not urgent"\n- Acknowledge wait time if SLA has been breached — own it\n- Use calm, decisive language when de-escalating angry customers\n- Never argue with a customer — redirect to resolution\n	escalation	[-0.059155907,0.039600305,0.020758936,-0.035586026,0.034689896,0.028770106,-0.030536348,0.03828022,0.0013670434,-0.020478705,0.040222708,-0.046977397,0.032021914,-0.044991404,0.12078658,-0.005900584,0.03444027,-0.024310207,-0.07725634,-0.053150985,0.06297069,-0.040507816,-0.06288879,0.072500356,-0.06805331,-0.019985689,-0.004285188,0.003777276,-0.05674304,-0.041185133,0.01471953,-0.0016628793,-0.026526086,0.053758726,-0.0043460564,0.035886817,0.0719187,-0.033541754,-0.045913316,-0.030360928,-0.0010286684,-0.07549394,-0.013692768,-0.004106533,0.06938096,0.012264452,-0.06151733,-0.009597551,-0.14305243,-0.013622605,0.0006355809,-0.040244985,-0.034206897,0.08501905,-0.042204857,0.0376613,0.054947324,-0.04002206,0.019505834,-0.058620337,-0.070001885,-0.029094866,0.0074908566,0.009303631,-0.102599435,0.033543568,0.035462003,0.0008068454,0.05873323,0.10017499,-0.02565385,-0.07018772,-0.055016037,0.062685825,-0.00996048,0.048655152,0.02171422,0.06148063,0.058184374,-0.086534314,-0.015264829,0.018470308,-0.025838383,0.0087408,-0.013856521,-0.07061225,-0.019738894,0.00436422,-0.006203617,0.028476277,0.08389201,-0.006350464,0.027991807,0.0075545036,0.027935907,0.04021655,-0.09389333,-0.12505017,0.04805375,-0.0034401664,0.013680261,0.032248087,0.010597232,-0.0021276185,-0.007606899,-0.042700175,0.025620844,0.03877361,-0.04581817,-0.022290528,-0.022407819,-0.083372906,0.047672946,-0.13809079,0.060236823,0.09294226,0.000812276,0.07339485,0.039977167,-0.049972225,0.075893685,0.010342476,-0.032761894,-0.018133461,-0.0036191123,0.015757997,0.017249884,1.0348553e-32,0.04378247,0.057321656,-0.085754596,0.058021344,0.08150348,0.0415597,0.046300624,0.034412783,-0.040192682,0.023709914,-0.03177596,0.035795,0.07403056,-0.024296958,-0.047901727,-0.07038632,-0.005211331,0.06664661,-0.024805