4	SOP: Customer Onboarding Support	# SOP: Customer Onboarding Support\n\n## Overview\nThis document defines how support agents handle onboarding-related tickets for new Luminnoz customers.\n\n## Onboarding Stages\n\n### Stage 1 — Account Setup (Days 1–3)\n- Invite team members\n- Configure workspace settings\n- Connect primary data source\n\n### Stage 2 — Integrations (Days 3–7)\n- Slack integration\n- CRM connection (Salesforce, HubSpot via Zapier)\n- API key generation and first API call\n\n### Stage 3 — First Value (Days 7–14)\n- Complete first workflow\n- Review dashboard with at least 50 data points\n- Schedule onboarding call with CSM (Growth and above)\n\n## Common Integration Issues\n\n### Slack Integration — Authorization Failed\n**Cause:** Slack workspace admin permissions not granted to the user attempting to connect.\n**Resolution:**\n1. Confirm the customer is a Slack Workspace Admin (not just a member)\n2. If not admin: ask them to have their Slack admin authorize the connection at Settings > Integrations > Luminnoz\n3. If admin: revoke and re-authorize at luminnoz.com/settings/integrations\n4. Clear browser cache and retry\n5. If still failing: collect browser console logs and escalate to Engineering\n\n### API Key Issues\n**Cause:** Key generated before workspace setup is complete.\n**Resolution:** Regenerate key after completing workspace setup. Old key is automatically invalidated.\n\n## Health Score Thresholds\n- Score < 50 and Day 7+: proactively reach out, offer onboarding call\n- Score < 30 at Day 14: flag for CSM review, risk of churn\n\n## Tone Guidelines\n- Onboarding tickets get same-day response regardless of tier\n- Use encouraging, patient tone — customer is still learning the product\n- Always end with a next step — never leave the customer without a clear action\n- Offer screen-share session for customers stuck more than 48 hours\n	onboarding	[-0.028300853,-0.062114682,-0.0545556,0.03135209,0.010365409,-0.05147043,0.03642942,0.04523508