5	SOP: Refund and Billing Dispute Policy	# SOP: Refund and Billing Dispute Policy\n\n## Overview\nThis document defines Luminnoz's refund policy and the process for handling billing disputes raised by customers.\n\n## Eligibility for Refunds\n\n### Automatic Refund (no approval needed)\n- Duplicate charge on the same billing cycle\n- System error confirmed by Engineering\n- Charge after confirmed cancellation date\n\n### Discretionary Refund (manager approval required)\n- Customer dissatisfaction within first 30 days (pro-rata)\n- Service outage exceeding 4 hours in a single month (credit, not refund)\n- Enterprise accounts: escalate to CSM before any commitment\n\n### Not Eligible\n- Charges older than 90 days (except duplicate charges)\n- Refund requests after active usage of the full billing period\n- Downgrade requests mid-cycle (effective next cycle)\n\n## Process\n\n### Step 1 — Verify the charge\n1. Access billing system and confirm the duplicate or erroneous charge\n2. Document: amount, date, invoice ID, and reason for error\n\n### Step 2 — Communicate timeline\n- Acknowledge within 1 business hour for enterprise accounts\n- Acknowledge within 4 business hours for growth/starter accounts\n- Refund processing time: 5–10 business days to original payment method\n\n### Step 3 — Apply resolution\n- Duplicate charge: issue full refund + apply $50 account credit as goodwill\n- System error: full refund + written apology from Support Lead\n- Enterprise disputes: loop in CSM before sending any resolution email\n\n## Escalation Triggers\n- Customer mentions legal action → escalate to Support Lead immediately\n- Customer mentions chargeback → escalate to Finance + Support Lead\n- Enterprise account + unresolved after 2 hours → page CSM on-call\n\n## Tone Guidelines\n- Always acknowledge the error directly — never minimize\n- Do not use the phrase "our records show" when the customer is clearly correct\n- Enterprise customers: address by first name, maintain formal register\n	billing	[-0.0995199,0.019067489,0.021002965,-0.0005041483,0.054516528,-0.04835932,-0.0034790176,0.057511296,-0.021989912,0.059277162,0.033396404,-0.018361349,0.034409795,-0.09478174,-0.037034877,-0.015064701,-0.02431835,0.008047372,-0.008372093,0.008093615,0.083839126,-0.05275477,-0.039787907,0.029534787,-0.009005509,0.014401191,-0.03485053,0.10264654,-0.03946139,-0.06464224,0.07097394,0.074669704,0.023225278,-0.07644801,0.05417591,0.047417037,0.005928238,-0.053939257,-0.013981534,-0.035913747,0.028369213,-0.035371568,-0.030704323,-0.048571315,0.057637453,0.00042988616,-0.091355376,0.036195826,-0.055908903,0.10306166,0.029833362,-0.06038628,0.0028331517,0.045461513,-0.040706966,0.0924188,0.03453432,0.026874948,-0.032950155,-0.040278744,-0.05605721,-0.037838783,-0.06130126,0.012075295,-0.054820012,0.08572297,-0.00873686,0.0052508083,-0.05492996,0.030748894,0.022935515,-0.025296709,-0.0659764,0.016178107,-0.018792966,0.019108975,0.031466696,0.067397304,-0.02773107,-0.08490456,-0.020588232,-0.019730363,-0.056145594,-0.032900464,0.018865777,-0.06357158,-0.020884944,0.07610943,0.06484872,-0.015588416,0.10746749,0.033576716,0.049274642,-0.05041323,0.028722815,0.06393432,-0.01517084,-0.0042255837,0.06613172,-0.0016209998,0.050936706,-0.0012029523,0.02331157,-0.052066397,0.030829567,-0.05873317,0.06051724,0.0068306844,-0.017415943,-0.039178576,0.042411685,-0.084627554,0.09505899,-0.041065488,0.07769212,0.07668155,-0.026400387,-0.018434068,0.045239218,-0.066451944,0.007998218,0.101004235,0.02117373,-0.06831002,-0.019779371,-0.01228631,0.05841895,9.9679416e-33,-0.037853934,0.02946297,-0.039451115,-0.07292921,0.051597863,0.029240614,0.078562014,0.07956228,-0.090126015,-0.0075931456,-0.044325307,0.056966066,0.030322844,-0.13767733,-0.16944309,-0.029489081,0.04151597,0.060104437,0.008649545,0.05560124,0.057666086,-0.0922324,0.020783914,0.018103236,0.032401662,0.01813669,0.019366207,-0.001322648,0.05951576,-0.015351626,0.046568945,0.006851814,0.015867496,0.079173386,-0.02